    "updated_at": "2024-07-30T20:41:41Z",
    "body": "> When attaching a declarative shadow root, if there is an error (for example, the tag name isn't valid, which the spec says results in a NotSupportedError DOMException, the spec says that the exception will be reported (i.e., an `error` event will be fired at the global object), but this doesn't seem to happen in any browser I tested. The error is logged in the console in Chrome, but no `error` event is fired.\r\n\r\nOops! Indeed I am just writing to the console rather than throwing an exception. Seems like this is just a browser bug, plus perhaps the lack of better WPTs for this case? I'm happy to fix both (at least for Chrome). Did you happen to file a crbug? Otherwise I will.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
