    "body": "The PR (now merged) says what seemed likely to be intended, that it go to the declarative shadow host element's relevant global object. In HTML there's no such thing as isolated worlds so this isn't really ambiguous (all platform objects have a single relevant realm). In Chromium/Blink, I would guess it should be the main world (`ToScriptStateForMainWorld`) in most cases (modulo cases where we know it was caused by script in an isolated world)?\r\n\r\nIf instead you think this shouldn't be reported to any global, then it should probably be modified to not use \"report an exception\" but instead just say that the UA might log it to the console?",
