    "created_at": "2024-08-08T08:30:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-08T08:30:58Z",
    "body": "In today's triage meeting we discussed this issue and @zcorpan's gut reaction was to go with console only (option 3). His reasoning was that it's unusual for the HTML parser to trigger script execution, and there's nonzero XSS risk if someone is able to inject a `<template>` element and trigger the page's `error` handler, which we believe is not currently something that can happen.\r\n\r\nNobody else had any strong opinions, so probably going with that option is the simplest thing to do.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
