    "created_at": "2024-08-08T18:30:23Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-08-08T18:30:49Z",
    "body": "Ohh, I hadn't thought about the XSS risk. That's totally valid and a bit scary.\r\n\r\nOk, thanks for discussing, and I'm fine with this conclusion. It seems like something needs to change in the spec, perhaps just [this section](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#parsing-main-inhead:concept-attach-a-shadow-root) should change to something like this?\r\n\r\n> [Attach a shadow root](https://dom.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-attach-a-shadow-root) with declarative shadow host element, mode, clonable, serializable, delegatesFocus, and \"named\". If an exception is thrown, then catch it, [insert an element at the adjusted insertion location](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#insert-an-element-at-the-adjusted-insertion-location) with template, and return.\r\n\r\nI.e. just remove \"[report](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#report-an-exception) it for declarative shadow host element's [relevant global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#concept-relevant-global)\" and leave the console errors to UAs.\r\n\r\nSound right? If so, I can put up a PR and also add some WPTs.",
